India has handed over four advanced life support ambulances to #Seychelles to strengthen bilateral cooperation in the health sector. 

High Commissioner of India to Seychelles, Rohit Rathish, handed over the ambulances to the country's Health Minister, Marvin Fanny.

@hci_seychelles said the gift reflects the people-centric nature of bilateral relations and the longstanding cooperation between the two countries in healthcare.

